1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,504
听：A Town Plans Its Water Supply.

2
00:00:03,504 --> 00:00:07,008
跟读：A Town Plans Its Water Supply.

3
00:00:07,008 --> 00:00:28,704
听：After a dry summer, a small town reviewed its water supply. The reservoir was lower than usual, and demand had increased as new homes were built. At a public meeting, an engineer explained that the town needed a plan for both ordinary use and a possible drought.

4
00:00:28,704 --> 00:00:50,400
跟读：After a dry summer, a small town reviewed its water supply. The reservoir was lower than usual, and demand had increased as new homes were built. At a public meeting, an engineer explained that the town needed a plan for both ordinary use and a possible drought.

5
00:00:50,400 --> 00:01:14,856
听：Water is collected, treated and distributed through a network of pipes. Some of those pipes had been installed many years earlier. A survey found leakage in several streets. Repairing the network would reduce waste, although the council still needed to compare the cost with other options.

6
00:01:14,856 --> 00:01:39,312
跟读：Water is collected, treated and distributed through a network of pipes. Some of those pipes had been installed many years earlier. A survey found leakage in several streets. Repairing the network would reduce waste, although the council still needed to compare the cost with other options.

7
00:01:39,312 --> 00:02:08,016
听：The engineer distinguished water conservation from water treatment. Filtration removes certain materials, while other stages deal with different forms of contamination. A proposed upgrade would be assessed before construction began. No one was asked to copy the treatment process at home; the discussion concerned the town's public infrastructure.

8
00:02:08,016 --> 00:02:36,720
跟读：The engineer distinguished water conservation from water treatment. Filtration removes certain materials, while other stages deal with different forms of contamination. A proposed upgrade would be assessed before construction began. No one was asked to copy the treatment process at home; the discussion concerned the town's public infrastructure.

9
00:02:36,720 --> 00:03:07,272
听：The council also invited farmers to discuss irrigation and seasonal demand. If rainfall remained low, restrictions might become necessary. Residents wanted a reliable supply without a large increase in charges. The final proposal combined pipe repairs, clearer information and a review of long-term capacity, rather than relying on a single solution.

10
00:03:07,272 --> 00:03:37,824
